1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,200
People say it is unfair to expect everyone to speak up against the injustices of the world.

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,400
And at one point I thought that was true.

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,020
But I know now that it is not.

4
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:21,060
I know now that the injustices of the world are committed by people who expect us to think that way.

5
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:30,520
They're the same people who told us don't share salary information so that they could be discriminatory in their salaries.

6
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:38,340
They're the same people that told us politics is personal so that we wouldn't come together as community and vote in our power.

7
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:48,120
They're the same people that tell us, you know, a woman's age is private because they want women to be shamed, to elevate, to mature, to be refined.

8
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:52,460
It is everybody's responsibility to speak up against injustice.

9
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:56,140
Not only those of us who are facing injustice, but those of us who are not.

10
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:02,840
If we are not responsible for that, then how do we expect injustice to not happen?

11
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,120
That is what being community is.

12
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:10,020
It is everyone working together for the betterment of everyone.

13
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:15,620
So if we don't consider it our business to speak up, then we do not consider ourselves community.

14
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:21,540
And that is exactly why they are able to do what they do to us, not just here in America, but globally.

15
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:25,580
The people who are doing injustice are speaking with actions.

16
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,000
The least we can do is speak with our voice.

